WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.670
To copper-plate a key,

2
00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:06.110
hang it in blue copper sulfate
solution and switch on the current.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.030
Copper ions are reduced onto the key,
and it turns a gleaming copper colour.

4
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.550
Copper ions are what
make the solution blue.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.090
So you might expect the blue
to fade as they're used up.

6
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.830
Yet hour after hour,
it stays just as blue.

7
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.890
Why doesn't the blue fade?

8
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:23.910
In this mission,

9
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.670
you'll predict what forms at each electrode
when copper sulfate solution is electrolysed.

10
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.190
You'll find out how electroplating works,

11
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.710
and write the half-equation
at each electrode.

12
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.080
Your mission: explain why the
copper sulfate solution stays blue.
